/**
 * ThemeProvider, replaced by nothing (kolonie-website#64).
 *
 * Starlight's own version writes `data-theme` onto `<html>` from
 * `localStorage`, falling back to `prefers-color-scheme`. That is the right
 * default for a documentation site that offers the choice. This site does not
 * offer it: the landing page has committed to one theme since `#30`, where it
 * is written into the markup rather than chosen at runtime.
 *
 * The result before this file existed was that a visitor on a light system read
 * a dark landing page and then a white document, on the click that matters
 * most — `#64` measured it across `/quests/`, `/skill`, `/academy/` and
 * `/who-builds-this`.
 *
 * **Rendering nothing is the whole fix, and it is not a trick.** `theme.css`
 * defines the dark set on `:root` and the light set on `:root[data-theme='light']`
 * only, and Starlight's own reset does the same for `color-scheme`. With
 * nothing writing the attribute, no selector in either file matches and the
 * dark set is what applies — statically, with no inline script and so no flash
 * of the wrong theme to avoid.
 *
 * **The light block stays in `theme.css` and is not dead.** It is what
 * `public/mark.svg` is checked against, and it is what the site would render
 * the day it offers the choice again. Deleting it would make restoring the
 * choice a redesign rather than a switch.
 *
 * `window.StarlightThemeProvider` is gone with the script. The only thing that
 * ever called it is Starlight's `ThemeSelect`, which this site renders nowhere —
 * see `ThemeSelect.astro` beside this file, which is what keeps that true.
 */
